# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial demonstrates how to run a utility-scale error mitigation "
"experiment with Qiskit Runtime using an experimental version of *zero-noise "
"extrapolation* (ZNE) with *probabilistic error amplification* (PEA).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dieses Tutorial zeigt, wie du mit Qiskit Runtime ein "
"Fehlerminderungsexperiment im Utility-Maßstab durchführst – unter Verwendung"
" einer experimentellen Version der *Zero-Noise-Extrapolation* (ZNE) mit "
"*probabilistischer Fehleramplifikation* (PEA).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![kim\\_nature\\_fig.png](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/e1e67c34-9d4d-4a88-9340-f0b2f3676770.avif)\n"
"**Reference**: Y. Kim et al. *Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance.* [Nature 618.7965 (2023)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3)\n"
msgstr ""
"![kim\\_nature\\_fig.png](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/e1e67c34-9d4d-4a88-9340-f0b2f3676770.avif)\n"
"**Referenz**: Y. Kim et al. *Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance.* [Nature 618.7965 (2023)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"
msgstr "Zero-Noise-Extrapolation (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is an error mitigation technique that removes"
" the effects of an *unknown* noise during circuit execution that can be "
"scaled in a *known* way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Zero-Noise-Extrapolation (ZNE) ist eine Fehlerminderungstechnik, die die "
"Auswirkungen eines *unbekannten* Rauschens während der Circuit-Ausführung "
"beseitigt, das sich auf eine *bekannte* Weise skalieren lässt.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It assumes expectation values scale with noise by a known function\n"
msgstr ""
"Sie geht davon aus, dass Erwartungswerte mit dem Rauschen gemäß einer "
"bekannten Funktion skalieren:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle A(\\lambda) \\rangle = \\langle A(0) \\rangle + \\sum_{k=0}^{m} a_k \\lambda^k + R\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle A(\\lambda) \\rangle = \\langle A(0) \\rangle + \\sum_{k=0}^{m} a_k \\lambda^k + R\n"
"$$\n"
"wobei $\\lambda$ die Rauschstärke parametrisiert und verstärkt werden kann.\n"
"ZNE lässt sich mit den folgenden Schritten umsetzen:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\lambda$ parameterizes the noise strength and can be amplified.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can implement ZNE with the following steps:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Amplify circuit noise for several noise factors $\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2, ..."
" $\n"
msgstr ""
"Verstärke das Circuit-Rauschen für mehrere Rauschfaktoren $\\lambda_1, "
"\\lambda_2, ... $\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run every noise-amplified circuit to measure $\\langle "
"A(\\lambda_1)\\rangle, ...$\n"
msgstr ""
"Führe jeden rauschverstärkten Circuit aus, um $\\langle "
"A(\\lambda_1)\\rangle, ...$ zu messen\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Extrapolate back to the zero-noise limit $\\langle A(0)\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "Extrapoliere zurück zur Zero-Noise-Grenze $\\langle A(0)\\rangle$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![zne\\_stages.png](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/images/tutorials/utility-"
"scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-"
"amplification/5e63d706-82d8-4212-b802-c9191ce53341.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![zne_stages.png](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/images/tutorials/utility-"
"scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-"
"amplification/5e63d706-82d8-4212-b802-c9191ce53341.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Amplify noise for ZNE {#amplify-noise-for-zne}"
msgstr "Rauschen für ZNE verstärken {#amplify-noise-for-zne}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The main challenge in successfully implementing ZNE is to have an accurate "
"model for noise in the expectation value and to amplify the noise in a known"
" way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Die größte Herausforderung bei der erfolgreichen Implementierung von ZNE "
"besteht darin, ein genaues Modell für das Rauschen im Erwartungswert zu "
"haben und das Rauschen auf bekannte Weise zu verstärken.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are three common ways error amplification is implemented for ZNE.\n"
msgstr "Es gibt drei gängige Methoden zur Fehleramplifikation für ZNE.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| **Pulse stretching**                                                                                                                                                                               | **Gate folding**                                                                                                                                                                               | **Probabilistic error amplification**                                                                                                                                                |\n"
"| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| Scale pulse duration via calibration                                                                                                                                                               | Repeat gates in identity cycles $U\\mapsto U(U^{-1}U)^{\\lambda-1}/2$                                                                                                                            | Add noise via sampling Pauli channels                                                                                                                                                |\n"
"| ![zne\\_pulse\\_stretching.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/83188b57-e88f-43a1-a7bd-29327f46ecf5.avif) | ![zne\\_gate\\_folding.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/e1358d08-2632-4fd2-bf0f-f9384a2d3340.avif) | ![zne\\_pea.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/3d69d5bd-70e5-4eeb-aa02-fc0a62043010.avif) |\n"
"| Kandala et al. Nature (2019)                                                                                                                                                                       | Shultz et al. PRA (2022)                                                                                                                                                                       | Li & Benjamin PRX (2017)                                                                                                                                                             |\n"
"For utility-scale experiments, *probabilistic error amplification* (PEA) is the most attractive.\n"
msgstr ""
"| **Puls-Dehnung** | **Gate-Faltung** | **Probabilistische Fehleramplifikation** |\n"
"|-----------|-----------|-----------|\n"
"| Skaliere die Pulsdauer per Kalibrierung | Wiederhole Gates in Identitätszyklen $U\\mapsto U(U^{-1}U)^{\\lambda-1}/2$ | Füge Rauschen durch Sampling von Pauli-Kanälen hinzu |\n"
"| ![zne_pulse_stretching.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/83188b57-e88f-43a1-a7bd-29327f46ecf5.avif) | ![zne_gate_folding.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/e1358d08-2632-4fd2-bf0f-f9384a2d3340.avif) | ![zne_pea.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/3d69d5bd-70e5-4eeb-aa02-fc0a62043010.avif) |\n"
"| Kandala et al. Nature (2019) | Shultz et al. PRA (2022) | Li & Benjamin PRX (2017) |\n"
"Für Experimente im Utility-Maßstab ist die *probabilistische Fehleramplifikation* (PEA) am attraktivsten.\n"
"- Puls-Dehnung setzt voraus, dass Gate-Rauschen proportional zur Dauer ist, was typischerweise nicht zutrifft. Außerdem ist die Kalibrierung aufwendig.\n"
"- Gate-Faltung erfordert große Streckfaktoren, die die Tiefe der ausführbaren Circuits stark einschränken.\n"
"- PEA kann auf jeden Circuit angewendet werden, der mit dem nativen Rauschfaktor ($\\lambda=1$) ausgeführt werden kann, erfordert jedoch das Erlernen des Rauschmodells.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pulse stretching assumes gate noise is proportional to duration, which is "
"typically not true. Calibration is also costly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Gate folding requires large stretch factors that greatly limit the depth of "
"circuits that can be run.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEA can be applied to any circuit that can be run with native noise factor "
"($\\lambda=1$) but requires learning the noise model.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise model for PEA {#learn-the-noise-model-for-pea}"
msgstr "Das Rauschmodell für PEA erlernen {#learn-the-noise-model-for-pea}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEA assumes the same layer-based noise model as *probabilistic error "
"cancellation* (PEC); however, it avoids the sampling overhead that scales "
"exponentially with the circuit noise.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| **Step 1**                                                                                                                                                                                       | **Step 2**                                                                                                                                                                                    | **Step 3**                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Pauli twirl layers of two-qubit gates                                                                                                                                                            | Repeat identity pairs of layers and learn the noise                                                                                                                                           | Derive a fidelity (error for each noise channel)                                                                                                                                                |\n"
"| ![pec\\_pauli\\_twirling.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/2eab5ff4-40fa-4a41-9f2c-74f5e22c4643.avif) | ![pec\\_learn\\_layer.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/8d0d64c3-65ad-4419-8ac9-4ec9633d39a0.avif) | ![pec\\_curve\\_fitting.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/c51bd42d-2463-4c78-807b-d284ca79296f.avif) |\n"
msgstr ""
"PEA setzt dasselbe schichtbasierte Rauschmodell wie *probabilistische Fehlerauslöschung* (PEC) voraus; es vermeidet jedoch den Sampling-Overhead, der exponentiell mit dem Circuit-Rauschen skaliert.\n"
"| **Schritt 1** | **Schritt 2** | **Schritt 3** |\n"
"|-----------|-----------|-----------|\n"
"| Pauli-Twirl-Schichten von Zwei-Qubit-Gates | Wiederhole Identitätspaare von Schichten und erlerne das Rauschen | Leite eine Fidelity ab (Fehler für jeden Rauschkanal) |\n"
"| ![pec_pauli_twirling.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/2eab5ff4-40fa-4a41-9f2c-74f5e22c4643.avif) | ![pec_learn_layer.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/8d0d64c3-65ad-4419-8ac9-4ec9633d39a0.avif) | ![pec_curve_fitting.png](/docs/images/tutorials/utility-scale-error-mitigation-with-probabilistic-error-amplification/c51bd42d-2463-4c78-807b-d284ca79296f.avif) |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Reference**: E. van den Berg, Z. Minev, A. Kandala, and K. Temme, "
"*Probabilistic error cancellation with sparse Pauli-Lindblad models on noisy"
" quantum processors* [arXiv:2201.09866](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866)\n"
msgstr ""
"__Referenz__: E. van den Berg, Z. Minev, A. Kandala, and K. Temme, "
"_Probabilistic error cancellation with sparse Pauli-Lindblad models on noisy"
" quantum processors_ [arXiv:2201.09866](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866)\n"

